From 6cb15139ad0170477967dc97bcf536c26e0e165d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 06:35:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] doc/examples/demux_decode: print audio timestamps in the
 stream time base

The pts of a decoded frame is expressed in the time base of the packets,
which is AVStream.time_base. output_audio_frame() converts it with
AVCodecContext.time_base instead, which is not set by the user when
decoding and happens to be 1/sample_rate for audio decoders. The printed
time is only right when the stream uses the same time base, as MP4
does. For AAC audio at 44100 Hz in MPEG-TS, where the time base is
1/90000, the first frame at 1.456778 seconds is printed as

    audio_frame n:0 nb_samples:1024 pts:2.973016

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FZ4G6798n6Ua4qu6xwWu3S
---
 doc/examples/demux_decode.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/doc/examples/demux_decode.c b/doc/examples/demux_decode.c
index a3a9131..a3602b3 100644
--- a/doc/examples/demux_decode.c
+++ b/doc/examples/demux_decode.c
@@ -92,7 +92,7 @@ static int output_audio_frame(AVFrame *frame)
     size_t unpadded_linesize = frame->nb_samples * av_get_bytes_per_sample(frame->format);
     printf("audio_frame n:%d nb_samples:%d pts:%s\n",
            audio_frame_count++, frame->nb_samples,
-           av_ts2timestr(frame->pts, &audio_dec_ctx->time_base));
+           av_ts2timestr(frame->pts, &audio_stream->time_base));
 
     /* Write the raw audio data samples of the first plane. This works
      * fine for packed formats (e.g. AV_SAMPLE_FMT_S16). However,
-- 
